2
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:44,200
皆さん、こんばんは！ハロー！
Good evening, everyone! Hello!

3
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:48,800
こんばんは！
Good evening!

4
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,600
はい！ということで、まずは自己紹介からやっていきましょう！
Alright! First off, let's introduce ourselves!

5
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:58,200
ホロライブの清楚担当、みんなのアイドル夏色まつりです！
I'm Natsuiro Matsuri, Hololive's pure and wholesome idol!

6
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:02,000
今日はMCを担当します。頑張ります！
I'll be your host today. I'll do my best!

7
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:08,500
じゃあ今日参加してくださる人たち1人ずつ行きますよ。
Next, let's have everyone introduce themselves one by one.

8
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:11,200
じゃあ、イオフィからお願いします！
Let me hand it over to Iofi first!

9
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:14,200
はい！イフォリア・オビサ！どうもです！
Hi! Ioforia obisa! Hello!

10
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:17,500
ホロライブインドネシアからイオフィです！
I'm Airani Iofi from Hololive Indonesia!

11
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:25,500
今日はオノマトペをちょっと…勉強したいと思います！
Today, I'd like to learn a bit about Japanese onomatopoeia!

12
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,500
よろしくお願いします！
Nice to meet you all!

13
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:30,000
よろしくお願いします！じゃあ、こぼちゃん！
Welcome! Next, Kobo-chan!

14
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Water water water, Kobo Kanaeru at your service! Let me be your sun to shine your day!

15
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
こぼ・かなえる、雨使いです！今日はオノマトペ…
I'm Kobo Kanaeru, the shaman of rain! Today's onomatopoeia...

16
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:46,000
ガチだ！お願いします！頑張ろう！
I'll give it my all! Nice to meet you! Let me at it!

17
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
ワー！
Yay!

18
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,500
じゃあ続いてジジ！
Next up is Gigi!

19
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,500
こんばんは！ジジです！
Good evening! I'm Gigi!

20
00:02:56,500 --> 00:03:01,500
日本語ちょっと上手じゃない…
My Japanese isn't that good yet...

21
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:08,500
オノマトペ、日本語頑張ります！
But I'll do my best with Japanese onomatopoeia!

22
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:12,500
ありがとう！頑張れー！
Thank you! Do your best!

23
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:16,800
じゃあ続いて、ほぼJPのベールズちゃん！
Next up, practically JP member Bae-chan!

24
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:21,000
いやいや！ホロライブEnglish、ハコス・ベールズです！
Hey now! I'm Hakos Baelz from Hololive English!

25
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:25,500
今日は翻訳担当で頑張りたいと思います！よろしくお願いします！
Today I'll do my best as the translator! Nice to meet you!

26
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:29,500
お願いします！
Welcome!

27
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,500
じゃあ最後、ラオラ！
And last but not least, Raora!

28
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:36,500
こんにちは！ラオラ・パンテーラです！
Hello! I'm Raora Panthera!

29
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:45,000
今日は絵を描いたり、日本語で話したり頑張りまーす！
Today I'll do my best drawing pictures and speaking Japanese!

30
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:51,000
はい、お願いします！
Great, welcome!

31
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:57,000
ということで、本日は皆さんにオノマトペクイズに答えてもらいます！
So today, everyone will be answering an onomatopoeia quiz!

32
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,000
日本独特の表現もたくさんあるんですが、頑張って答えてね。
There are many unique Japanese expressions, so do your best!

33
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:11,500
ぜひ日本に来る際は、いっぱい使っていただきたいなと思います！
I hope you can use them a lot when you visit Japan!

34
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:14,500
はい！ということで！
Alright then!

35
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:17,500
さっそく第1問行きましょう！
Let me present Question 1!

36
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:23,500
クエスチョン1！
Question 1!

37
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:31,500
このオノマトペは何を表しているでしょうか？「コケコッコー」
What does this onomatopoeia represent? "Kokekokko"

38
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:39,000
あ、What is this sound? コケコッコー
Ah, what is this sound? "Kokekokko"

39
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Where do you hear this onomatopoeia from?

40
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,000
分からない！
I don't know!

41
00:04:51,000 --> 00:05:00,000
ヒントは、動物の鳴き声ですね。なんの動物の鳴き声でしょう？
Here's a hint: it's an animal sound. What animal sound is it?

42
00:05:02,008 --> 00:05:06,308
ペンがおかしいんです、私。なんで？
My pen... My pen is acting weird. Why?

43
00:05:06,508 --> 00:05:08,508
え？おかしい？
Huh? It's weird?

44
00:05:09,508 --> 00:05:13,508
コケコッコー
Cock-a-doodle-doo.

45
00:05:17,508 --> 00:05:20,008
ペンがおかしい...あれ、なんでこんな...
My pen is weird... Huh, why is it like this?

46
00:05:20,208 --> 00:05:23,008
描けるかな？
I wonder if I can draw?

47
00:05:23,208 --> 00:05:26,008
あ、ちょっと待ってください。アプリ再起動します。
Ah, wait a second. I'm going to restart the app.

48
00:05:26,508 --> 00:05:28,008
Should we draw?

49
00:05:28,108 --> 00:05:30,008
You can do whatever.

50
00:05:30,108 --> 00:05:34,508
I drew because I don't know what it is in Japanese.

51
00:05:36,008 --> 00:05:37,808
I don't know the word!

52
00:05:38,208 --> 00:05:40,008
なん、何ですか？
Wh-What is it?

53
00:05:40,508 --> 00:05:42,008
描けるかな？
Can I draw it?

54
00:05:43,208 --> 00:05:45,508
あ、描けます！あ、よかった！
Ah, I can draw! Ah, thank goodness!

55
00:05:45,808 --> 00:05:48,008
よかったー。
Thank goodness!

56
00:05:50,808 --> 00:05:53,008
声に出したらわかるかも。
Saying it out loud might help you figure it out.

57
00:05:56,008 --> 00:05:57,208
遠い！
So far off!

58
00:05:57,508 --> 00:05:59,008
大丈夫かい？
Are you okay?

59
00:05:59,508 --> 00:06:03,508
コケコッコーですよ。
It's "cock-a-doodle-doo."

60
00:06:05,508 --> 00:06:08,508
オッケー、じゃあ1人ずつ聞いていきましょう！
Okay, let's ask everyone one by one!

61
00:06:09,008 --> 00:06:12,008
じゃあ、よっぴぴ！何だと思いますか？
Okay, Yoppipi! What do you think it is?

62
00:06:13,008 --> 00:06:14,508
あ、チキンです！
Ah, chicken!

63
00:06:14,608 --> 00:06:18,008
あ、チキン！はいはいはい、ニワトリね！
Ah, chicken! Right, right, right, a chicken!

64
00:06:18,808 --> 00:06:21,008
はい、じゃあ、えー、コボちゃん！
Okay, next up, Kobo-chan!

65
00:06:22,008 --> 00:06:25,508
Before I was thinking about frog,

66
00:06:25,608 --> 00:06:28,008
but I think "kekokeko",

67
00:06:28,108 --> 00:06:33,508
it sounds like Indonesian "kukuruyuk"!

68
00:06:33,608 --> 00:06:35,008
So it's chicken!

69
00:06:35,208 --> 00:06:37,508
あー、なるほど！
Ah, I see!

70
00:06:38,508 --> 00:06:41,008
元々カエルだと思ってたんだけど、
She originally thought it was a frog,

71
00:06:41,108 --> 00:06:44,008
インドネシアのオノマトペでも...
but even in Indonesian onomatopoeia...

72
00:06:44,108 --> 00:06:48,008
オノマトペ...オノマトペ...
Onomatopoeia... Onomatopoeia...

73
00:06:53,008 --> 00:06:58,008
ニワトリの声に似てるので、チキン！なるほどね。
...it sounds like a rooster's crow, so chicken! I see.

74
00:07:00,008 --> 00:07:01,508
はい、じゃあジジ！
Okay, next up, Gigi!

75
00:07:01,808 --> 00:07:06,508
「コケコッコー」、英語は Cock-a-doodle-doo!
"Kokekokko", in English it's "Cock-a-doodle-doo!"

76
00:07:06,608 --> 00:07:07,808
Chicken!

77
00:07:08,508 --> 00:07:11,008
Cock-a-doodle-doo！同じだね！
"Cock-a-doodle-doo!" So it's the same!

78
00:07:11,208 --> 00:07:12,508
じゃあ、ベッちゃん！
Next, Bae-chan!

79
00:07:13,008 --> 00:07:16,508
あ、僕もニワトリ、チキンだと思います！
Ah, I also think it's a chicken!

80
00:07:16,608 --> 00:07:18,008
チキン！
Chicken!

81
00:07:18,208 --> 00:07:19,508
じゃあ最後、ラーナ！
And lastly, Raora!

82
00:07:20,508 --> 00:07:24,008
For me, it's like a bird that is screaming like...

83
00:07:24,108 --> 00:07:27,508
"Coco!" Like "I'm here!" and...

84
00:07:29,008 --> 00:07:35,508
...wants food in its mouth because maybe it's small, you know.

85
00:07:38,508 --> 00:07:40,008
Wait, so what do you think it is?

86
00:07:41,008 --> 00:07:44,008
Screaming bird... 叫ぶ鳥...
Screaming bird... Screaming bird...

87
00:07:44,508 --> 00:07:47,008
叫ぶ鳥ね！
A screaming bird, huh?

88
00:07:47,208 --> 00:07:50,008
叫ぶ鳥ね！
A screaming bird, right!

89
00:07:50,508 --> 00:07:53,508
お腹空いてる叫ぶ鳥ね！
A hungry screaming bird!

90
00:07:54,008 --> 00:07:55,208
妖怪！
A monster!

91
00:07:55,508 --> 00:07:58,508
じゃあ正解いきましょう！正解は...
Now then, let's reveal the answer! The answer is...

92
00:07:58,808 --> 00:08:01,008
チキン、ニワトリでしたー！
Chicken, it was a chicken!

93
00:08:01,508 --> 00:08:03,008
You got it!

94
00:08:03,108 --> 00:08:04,508
やったー！
Yay!

95
00:08:08,008 --> 00:08:11,008
まぁ、正解にしますか！叫ぶ鳥だもんね！
Well, let's count it as correct! It is a screaming bird after all!

96
00:08:12,508 --> 00:08:16,508
鳥は鳥だからね！同じだからね！
A bird is a bird! It's basically the same thing!

97
00:08:17,008 --> 00:08:18,508
素晴らしい！
Wonderful!

98
00:08:19,008 --> 00:08:20,508
Everybody gets a point!

99
00:08:22,508 --> 00:08:27,508
コケコッコー！
Cock-a-doodle-doo!

100
00:08:31,008 --> 00:08:36,508
はい、じゃあ続いて第2問！こちらも動物の鳴き声でございます。
Alright, moving on to Question 2! This one is also an animal sound.

101
00:08:37,008 --> 00:08:40,808
The second question is also the sound of an animal.

102
00:08:41,208 --> 00:08:44,008
じゃあ第2問はこちら！ケロケロ！
Here is Question 2! "Kero kero!"

103
00:08:45,008 --> 00:08:48,008
ケロケロ！
"Kero kero!"

104
00:08:48,208 --> 00:08:50,008
Easy! Easy!

105
00:08:50,508 --> 00:08:55,008
Easy, easy!

106
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:56,508
ケロケロ。
"Kero kero."

107
00:08:59,008 --> 00:09:01,008
描けるかな？
Can you draw it?

108
00:09:04,008 --> 00:09:06,008
ベーちゃん、それは...
Bae-chan, that is...

109
00:09:06,208 --> 00:09:08,008
え？え？すごい！
Huh? Huh? Amazing!

110
00:09:10,008 --> 00:09:12,508
何何何？
What is that?

111
00:09:14,208 --> 00:09:16,008
Hey, my pen...

112
00:09:18,008 --> 00:09:22,008
ケロケロケロケロ...
"Kero kero kero kero..."

113
00:09:23,008 --> 00:09:26,508
可愛い！描けるかな？
Cute! Can you draw it?

114
00:09:27,008 --> 00:09:28,508
ローラ、大丈夫？
Raora, are you okay?

115
00:09:29,008 --> 00:09:33,008
あ、大丈夫。Okay, it's working. Thank you.
Ah, I'm okay. Okay, it's working. Thank you.

116
00:09:36,008 --> 00:09:39,008
ベーちゃんのは何？え？
What is Bae-chan's drawing? Huh?

117
00:09:41,008 --> 00:09:43,008
Hold on, I forgot what it looked like!

118
00:09:44,508 --> 00:09:46,508
What are you drawing?

119
00:09:46,808 --> 00:09:48,508
Why is she drawing herself?

120
00:09:48,808 --> 00:09:51,508
I forgot what it looked like!

121
00:09:55,508 --> 00:09:57,008
画伯！
Master artist!

122
00:09:57,208 --> 00:09:59,808
It's like a chimera, you know? キメラみたい。
It's like a chimera, you know? It looks like a chimera.

123
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:01,216
キメラ...
Chimera...

124
00:10:01,216 --> 00:10:03,016
キマイラなのやめて
Stop saying Chimera!

125
00:10:03,316 --> 00:10:07,516
おいっちゃん、ちょっと1人ずつまた聞いていきますか。かわいいみんな。
Shall we ask each person one by one again? Everyone's so cute.

126
00:10:09,116 --> 00:10:11,216
えー、じゃあ、イオフィ！
Uh, then, Iofi!

127
00:10:11,816 --> 00:10:12,716
はい！
Yes!

128
00:10:12,816 --> 00:10:14,616
カエル！Frogです。
Kaeru! It's frog.

129
00:10:14,816 --> 00:10:17,816
ああ、Frog！ケロ、ケロケロでしょ？
Ah, frog! Kerokero, right?

130
00:10:18,516 --> 00:10:20,216
その通り！はい！
Exactly! Yes!

131
00:10:20,516 --> 00:10:22,516
じゃあ、続いて、こぼちゃん！
Next up, Kobo-chan!

132
00:10:23,016 --> 00:10:28,016
あたしも、カエル... Frog, Frog, カエル、はい！ケロケロ！
Me too, frog... Frog, frog, kaeru, yes! Kerokero!

133
00:10:28,516 --> 00:10:30,816
漢字で書いてる！すごーい！
She wrote it in kanji! Amazing!

134
00:10:34,016 --> 00:10:36,016
まつりも書けないよ、カエル。
Even Matsuri can't write "frog" in kanji.

135
00:10:37,516 --> 00:10:39,216
じゃあ、続いてジジ！
Next up, Gigi!

136
00:10:39,516 --> 00:10:42,216
はい！ケロケロ、ケロッピ！
Yes! Kerokero Keroppi!

137
00:10:42,516 --> 00:10:45,016
あ、ケロケロケロッピ！おー！
Ah, Kerokero Keroppi! Oooh!

138
00:10:46,016 --> 00:10:48,016
じゃあ、ベーちゃん！
Next, Bae-chan!

139
00:10:48,816 --> 00:10:52,516
あ、カエルです。カエルかな？カエルです！
Ah, it's a frog. Is it a frog? It's a frog!

140
00:10:56,516 --> 00:10:59,816
一瞬ずっとね、ネズミみたいに書いてたんだけど...
For a moment, she was drawing it like a mouse...

141
00:11:01,016 --> 00:11:03,816
さっきね、カエル見たことないんで...
Actually, I've never seen a frog before...

142
00:11:04,516 --> 00:11:06,516
画伯だ！
Quite the artist!

143
00:11:07,016 --> 00:11:10,016
その隣の、えー、ラオーラ！めっちゃうまい！
Next to her, Raora! She's super good!

144
00:11:10,516 --> 00:11:13,516
可愛い！可愛い！
So cute! So cute!

145
00:11:14,516 --> 00:11:16,816
カエルですね？
It's a frog, right?

146
00:11:17,516 --> 00:11:20,016
カエルです！
It's a frog!

147
00:11:20,516 --> 00:11:25,016
じゃあ、ケロケロ、正解は... カエルでございます！
Now then, kerokero... The correct answer is... Frog!

148
00:11:25,516 --> 00:11:30,016
正解！
Correct!

149
00:11:30,216 --> 00:11:33,816
Easy! Easy! よかったー！
Easy! Easy! So glad!

150
00:11:34,516 --> 00:11:37,516
日本語上手！日本語上手よ！
Your Japanese is so good! You guys are great at Japanese!

151
00:11:38,516 --> 00:11:41,516
じゃあ続いていきますよ。続いては、えー、こちら！
Now then, let's move on. Next up is... this!

152
00:11:44,016 --> 00:11:48,016
「馬の鳴き声は？」日本だと何と言うでしょう？
"What sound does a horse make?" What is it in Japan?

153
00:11:48,216 --> 00:11:53,816
What sound does a horse make? Japanese onomatopoeia.

154
00:11:55,016 --> 00:11:58,016
分からない！
I don't know!

155
00:11:58,216 --> 00:12:01,516
なんて聞こえるかなー？
How does it sound to you guys?

156
00:12:08,516 --> 00:12:12,016
イメージ、イメージして！
Imagine it, picture it!

157
00:12:15,016 --> 00:12:19,016
It's alright Gigi, feel it from your heart!

158
00:12:19,216 --> 00:12:20,816
You can do it!

159
00:12:21,016 --> 00:12:23,816
1人ずつ鳴いてもらうからね！
Everyone will make their sound one by one!

160
00:12:24,016 --> 00:12:31,516
She's gonna ask each of you to sound out the onomatopoeia that you have come up with.

161
00:12:35,016 --> 00:12:37,016
オッケー？
Okay?

162
00:12:37,216 --> 00:12:39,516
全然知らん...
I have no idea...

163
00:12:40,516 --> 00:12:43,016
じゃあ、1人ずつ鳴いてもらえますか？
Now then, can everyone make their sound one by one?

164
00:12:43,216 --> 00:12:48,016
じゃあ、イオフィから！イオフィの馬の鳴き声、お願いします！
Let's start with Iofi! Iofi, please give us your horse sound!

165
00:12:49,016 --> 00:12:51,516
張り切っていこう！です！
It's "Let's go full power!"!

166
00:12:52,016 --> 00:12:54,816
張り切っていこう？それ違くて！
"Let's go full power"? That's not it!

167
00:12:57,016 --> 00:13:00,216
